This paper explores the existence of weak solutions to the following type of elliptic equation in the context of a complete Riemannian manifold $M$: 

$$
  -\text{div}\left(\frac{\partial_t u}{|\nabla u|^{p(t)-2}}\nabla u\right)+\text{div}\left(
  \frac{|u|^{
  q(t)-2}
  F(t)|\nabla u|^{q(t)}-
  F(t)|u|^{q(t)}
  )\right]=2u
  $$

  where $p(t)$ and $q(t)$ are continuous functions that vary within certain constraints, and $F(t)$ is a given function, with the authors establishing the existence of solutions for a broad class of functions $p(t)$ and $q(t)$, and extending previous results in the Euclidean setting to the Riemannian manifold setting.
